# Day 22 Notes — Transaction Status Audit History

## Objective

Implement a permanent audit trail for every transaction status change.

Previously, the `TRANSACTIONS` table stored only the current status. After Day 22, the platform can show the complete transaction lifecycle.

## Status lifecycle

A successful transaction follows:

```text
NULL → PENDING → PROCESSING → COMPLETED
```

Other possible transitions include:

```text
PROCESSING → FAILED
PROCESSING → RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED
RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED → COMPLETED
RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED → MANUAL_REVIEW
```

## Database migration

Created:

```text
V5__create_transaction_status_history.sql
```

New table:

```text
TRANSACTION_STATUS_HISTORY
```

It stores:

- Status-history ID
- Transaction ID
- Transaction reference
- Previous status
- New status
- Transition source
- Transition reason
- Correlation ID
- Creation timestamp

The history table is append-only: each transition creates a new record instead of overwriting earlier records.

## New transition-source enum

Created `TransactionTransitionSource`:

```java
TRANSACTION_SUBMISSION
TRANSACTION_PROCESSOR
RECONCILIATION_API
RECONCILIATION_SCHEDULER
MANUAL_REVIEW
```

It identifies which application process caused a status change.

## New history entity and repository

Created:

```text
TransactionStatusHistory
TransactionStatusHistoryRepository
```

The repository retrieves history chronologically:

```java
findByTransactionReferenceOrderByCreatedAtAscStatusHistoryIdAsc(...)
```

The secondary sort by history ID gives deterministic ordering when two records have similar timestamps.

## Centralized transition service

Created:

```text
TransactionStatusTransitionService
```

Important methods:

```java
saveInitialTransaction(...)
```

Saves the new transaction and writes:

```text
NULL → PENDING
```

```java
transition(...)
```

Updates the transaction status and writes the corresponding history record.

Both operations use `@Transactional`, ensuring that the transaction update and audit-history insert commit or roll back together.

## Duplicate transition handling

If the transaction already has the requested status:

```java
previousStatus == newStatus
```

the service returns the transaction without inserting duplicate history.

This prevents repeated reconciliation calls from creating meaningless history rows.

## Transition reason validation

Transition reasons are:

- Trimmed before persistence
- Converted to `null` when blank
- Limited to 500 characters

Invalid reasons are rejected before database operations occur.

## Transaction processing updates

`TransactionService` now uses the centralized transition service for:

- Initial transaction creation
- `PENDING → PROCESSING`
- `PROCESSING → COMPLETED`
- `PROCESSING → FAILED`
- Moving unresolved transactions to reconciliation

This prevents status changes from bypassing audit-history creation.

## Reconciliation updates

Manual API reconciliation uses:

```java
RECONCILIATION_API
```

Scheduled reconciliation uses:

```java
RECONCILIATION_SCHEDULER
```

Transactions moved to manual review are also recorded through the transition service.

## History API

Added:

```http
GET /api/v1/transactions/{transactionReference}/history
```

It returns the complete ordered transaction status history.

Supporting classes:

```text
TransactionStatusHistoryResponse
TransactionStatusHistoryService
```

## Correlation ID tracking

The transition service reads the correlation ID from SLF4J MDC:

```java
MDC.get("correlationId")
```

It stores that value in every status-history row, connecting:

```text
API request → logs → transaction → status changes
```

