## Verified Oracle result

The tested transaction produced:

| Previous status | New status | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `NULL` | `PENDING` | `TRANSACTION_SUBMISSION` |
| `PENDING` | `PROCESSING` | `TRANSACTION_PROCESSOR` |
| `PROCESSING` | `COMPLETED` | `TRANSACTION_PROCESSOR` |

The database also stored transition reasons, timestamps, transaction identifiers, and the correlation ID.

## Interview explanation

“On Day 22, I implemented a transaction status audit trail. Instead of storing only the latest status, every transition is appended to a history table with its previous and new status, transition source, reason, timestamp, and correlation ID. I centralized all status updates in a transactional service so the business update and audit record commit or roll back together. I also exposed an API to retrieve the complete lifecycle and added unit tests for transition behavior and validation.